                    The Wandering Jew: Drama, Opera, Film, etc

Alexandre, Maxime. 
  _Le Juif errant, trois actes, prologue et intermede_.
  Paris, Gallimard, 1946, 119p. 

Dore, Gustave, 1832-1883.
  _The Legend of the Wandering Jew: a series of twelve designs with
explanatory introduction_. (With doggerel under each engraving).
  London/New York. Cassell, Petter & Galpin, 1866, vii, 12 pl. 
  Philadelphia, G. Gebbie, 1873, 15 p, 12 pl.

Fragerolle, Georges Auguste (1855-1920).
  _Le juif errant, legende en 8 tableaux_. Poeme et musique de G.
Fragerolle ; dessins de Henri Riviere (1864-1951). 
  Paris, Enoch, E. Flammarion, 1898, 1 vocal score, 44 p.

Franklin, Andrew, ?-1845.
  _The Wandering Jew; or, Love's Masquerade: a Comedy in Two Acts_.
  London, George Cawthorn, 1797, 55 p.
  4th edition, 1797, in _British theatre. Comedies._ v.7

Haupt, Th(eodor) von, 1784-1832.
  _Ahasverus der nie Ruhende: romantisches Schauspiel in dreiAbtheilungen_.
Based on Louis Charles Caigniez' _Le Juif errant_ (Paris, 1812). 
  Mainz, F. Kupferberg, 1825, 56 p.

Heath, Charles, 1785-1848.
  _Heath's illustrations to The Wandering Jew [by Eugene Sue] drawn by the
first artists in Paris ; and executed on wood by the most eminent English
engravers_. Published to accompany the Chapman and Hall translation of
Eugene Sue's _Le Juif errant_, as first issued in 78 [sic] parts. 
  London, Chapman and Hall, 1845-1846. 26 pts in 1 v.

Heijermans, Herman, 1864-1924.
  _Ahasver. Schauspiel in einem Aufzug_. Einzig berechtigte Ubersetzung
aus dem Hollandischen von Paul Rache [1869-?]_. 
  Leipzig, P. Reclam jun, 1904, 32p. (series: Universal-Biboliothek, 4615)

Jens, Walter, 1923-.
  _Ahasver_ (radio play)
  Hamburg, Verlag Hans Bredow-Institut, 1956 and 1962, 40p. (Series:
Horwerke der Zeit ; 6.)

Jens, Walter, 1923-.
  _Ahasver; der Weg eines Verfemten durch Diktatur und Krieg_.
  Deutscher Theaterverlag, 1972?, 47p. (Series: Leseszenen und Lesespiele
Heft 69/70.)

Joly, Vincent, called Victor, 1811-1870.
  _Le Juif errant: mystification fantastique en trois tableaux par M. 
Jacob_. "Representee pour la premiere fois sur le Theatre des folies
dramatiques, le 25 octobre 1834." 
  Paris, Marchant, 1834, 15p. (series: Le magasin theatral; t. 4, no. 10.)

Klingemann, August, 1777-1831.
  _Ahasver. Trauerspiel in funf Acten_.
  Braunschweig, G.C.E. Meyer, 1827, 126p.

Kuprian, Hermann, 1920-.
  _Ahasver: Einakterzyklus in 6 Teilen_.
  Innsbruck, Universitatsverlag Wagner, 1984, 151 p. ISBN 3703001348
(series: Dramatiker, Stucke, Perspektiven)

Morpurgo, Salomone, 1860-1942.
  _L'ebreo errante [in Italia]_.
  Florence, Libreria Dante, 1891, 54p. (series: Collezione de operette
edite ed inedite 15). 
  Firenze, Arnaldo Forni, 1983, 54p.

Thurston, Ernest Temple, 1879-1933.
  _The Wandering Jew; a play on four phases_.
  New York, London, G. P. Putnam's sons, 1921, viii, 156 p.

_The Wandering Jew_. (Motion picture) 1905, silent, 1 reel ca. 400ft.

_The Wandering Jew_. (Motion picture) 1933, directed by Maurice Elvey,
cinematography by Sydney Blythe, written by H. Fowler Mear, starring Peggy
Ashcroft, Felix Aylmer, Marie Ney, John Stuart, Francis L. Sullivan,
Conrad Veidt.

Wandor, Michelene, 1940-, and Alfreds, Mike.
  _The Wandering Jew: adapted from Eugene Sue's [1804-1857] French classic_.
  London, New York, Methuen, 1987. 72 p. (series: Methuen's new
theatrescripts) ISBN 0413179206

